course: dictionary
lesson: 5816
title: Magnificent: grand, or simply excellent
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Magnificent is a big, showy word. It means very beautiful, grand and impressive. «The palace was magnificent, with gold domes and marble halls.» The clues are gold domes and marble halls, so you can tell the word is about something splendid to look at.
explain: People also use magnificent in everyday talk, to mean extremely good or excellent. «You were magnificent!» said after a school play does not mean the actor was beautiful. It means the performance was excellent. Read the words around the word to check which meaning fits.
explain: Magnificent can describe many things: a view, a costume, a building or a performance. Common phrases are «a magnificent view» and «simply magnificent». Try swapping in grand or excellent: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Magnificent means very beautiful, grand and impressive.
fact: Informally, magnificent means extremely good or excellent, as in «You were magnificent!»
fact: Magnificent is an adjective. Its adverb is magnificently.
fact: «Suleiman the Magnificent» was a great Ottoman sultan who ruled the Ottoman Empire at its height in the 1500s.
fact: Suleiman was famous for his laws and great mosques, and his name shows how grand and impressive people thought he was.
exercise: «Suleiman the Magnificent ruled the Ottoman Empire in the 1500s.» What does magnificent mean in this name? | Very quiet | Very tired | *Grand and impressive | Lost and alone
exercise: Dad says, «You were magnificent in the football match!» What does he mean? | You were wearing a costume | You were late for the match | You were very beautiful to look at | *You played extremely well
exercise: Which word is the adverb of magnificent? | magnificent | magnify | *magnificently
test: «The view from the top of the hill was magnificent.» What does magnificent mean here? | Very small and quiet | Dirty and dark | Cold and wet | *Very beautiful, grand and impressive
test: Which phrase uses magnificent to mean beautiful and grand? | a wet sock | a crumb on the floor | *a magnificent view
exam: Toad says, «What carts I shall fling carelessly into the ditch in the wake of my magnificent onset!» In his words, what does magnificent mean? | *Grand and impressive | Wet and cold | Small and quiet | Late and slow
